{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1550827-fantasy-game","id":1550827,"title":"Fantasy Game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-07T20:22:05-07:00","id":1550827,"title":"Fantasy Game?","content":"Has anyone ran a fantasy-game in CoD?<br /> <br /> I just thought of a fantasy-game for CoD, but, with no major-splats; so, no werewolves, vampires or mages etc. Just out of the basic rule-book; the only magic would be hedge or psychic-powers. (But, then again, the Purified and Spirits, would exist). <br /> <br /> When V:tM came out, we ran Forgotten Realms to WoD's rules, and it was, unusual. We tried to balance out the, &quot;Clases&quot;, but, it didn't; then, we got Mage:tA, and to heck with balance, Mages use real Magik: If you want to be a fighter, you put your skills in melee etc. Now, that was a fun game! <br /> <br /> And Sorcerer's Crusade would have worked better, but, by the time it came out, we weren't into the Mage mega-plot (technocracy vs. traditions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T08:32:42-07:00","id":1550842,"title":"","content":"No, though it's been on my to-do pile for years. Always fancied doing an <i>Awakening</i> game in a fantasy world; basically <i>To The Strongest</i> without the quiescence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T11:51:14-07:00","id":1550847,"title":"","content":"I have, but it wasn't without splats. It was a Werewolf the Forsaken game. The werewolves kept up their masquerade but enemies like spirits and claimed were open about their existence.<br /> <br /> In the Mirrors book there's a section with suggestions for building a fantasy world that contain write-ups for the converted Vampires, Werewolves, and Mages, as well as advice for populating it with peoples and different ways to explain magic. There is even a new template for mortals, &quot;Dark Heroes,&quot; and the city-setting of Woundgate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T10:50:55-07:00","id":1550962,"title":"","content":"The first chronicle I played was a fantasy game based on Final Fantasy using WoD's system. It was fun, and I run a few sessions in it too.<br /> <br /> But CoD, I have run three chronicles of Pokemon using it. It did had splats, though, as Pokemon is a setting where strange people do exist. No Masquerade, though, and the stars of the show were the Pokemon. It was a success every time. I'm working again on my adaptation, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T17:44:12-07:00","id":1550979,"title":"","content":"In the middle of a campaing. Were using a PF adventure as a guide, but were doing lots of twists to not escalate too much. Players are an Awakened, a Kindred and a Lost. Since the focus is more on the fantasy and adventure side of things, lots of major rules have been revamped.<br /> <br /> Kindred does not have sunlight bane. Awakened magic can be seen by everyone(including nimbus while casting something), paradox is more strain and less &quot;abyssal influence&quot;, no Keeper to drag the Lost back, but people generally mistrust those who have &quot;fairy blood&quot;. And lots of other tweaks to make this work. Not perfect, but still fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-08T19:10:33-07:00","id":1554251,"title":"","content":"I have ASoI&amp;F: RPG; it's nice, but I don't really understand the game-mechanics (but, how to design your own House, made a lot of sense). The more I think of it, CoD, is a lot like the books. Magic is limited, like, merit based and I'd use Second Sight and Spirits. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1550827-fantasy-game?p=1550979#post1550979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the middle of a campaing. Were using a PF adventure as a guide, but were doing lots of twists to not escalate too much. Players are an Awakened, a Kindred and a Lost. Since the focus is more on the fantasy and adventure side of things, lots of major rules have been revamped.. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>PF? Palladium Fantasy? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-21T11:39:03-07:00","id":1554548,"title":"","content":"I had worked on a game. Based on Avatar: the Last Airbender before using nWoD rules. That was pretty fantasy, all humans no splats, but with some extensive modifications and new powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27512-next_raven","name":"Next_Raven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}